{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And the king</b> — some say: it is Saul. The correct in my eyes: it is David." "And the sense of all: <b>who swears by Him</b> in truth, like <b>every tongue shall swear</b>, and it is the opposite of <b>a mouth of speakers of falsehood</b>." "Some say: the sense of <b>who swears by Him</b> — on account of Saul's oath."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 63, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:38.896237788Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}